---
import CabinetPage from '../layouts/CabinetPage.astro';
---

<CabinetPage
  title="Methodology — ecommarketdata"
  description="How Ecom Market Data collects, verifies and updates ecommerce marketplace datasets."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Methodology</p>
      <div class="prose">
        <h1>How we collect and verify data</h1>

        <p>
          Every dataset on this site follows the same process. If a number cannot
          be verified, it is not published.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Scope</h2>
        <p>
          Each dataset defines one metric, one market and one period. We do not
          mix definitions across pages, because a GMV figure is only comparable
          to another GMV figure measured the same way.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Collection</h2>
        <p>
          Data comes from public marketplace listings, official platform
          statements, financial disclosures and structured observation of public
          pages. Where a figure is estimated, the page says so.
        </p>

        <h2>3. Verification</h2>
        <p>Before publication, a figure must pass three checks:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>It can be traced to a named source.</li>
          <li>It is consistent with the previous period unless a change is explained.</li>
          <li>It is dated and scoped to a specific market.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. Updates</h2>
        <p>
          Each page carries a last-updated date. When a figure changes, the page
          changes and the date moves. We do not silently overwrite history.
        </p>

        <h2>5. Corrections</h2>
        <p>
          If you find an error, contact us. Verified corrections are applied and
          noted on the page.
        </p>

        <h2>Limitations</h2>
        <p>
          Marketplace data is often estimated from public signals rather than
          reported by the platforms themselves. Treat figures as best-available
          estimates, not audited financials.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</CabinetPage>
